476-477	751,889,1703,2030 - 1505,940,1660,1142 - 1118,1234,1158,1259 - 1390,1570,1536,1760 - 1557,1569,1688,1760 - 882,1828,1030,2030 - 904,1793,1030,1828 - 1540,1797,1683,2030 - 1527,1797,1540,1988	476. Summit of a flowering branch of Pokeweed. 477. Fruit-bearing branch.	One block: at upper left, 476, a leafy branch-tip with a slender raceme of small flowers; behind it, 477, a tall stem with alternate leaves and drooping racemes of round berries.
478	1509,947,1655,1139 - 1598,1095,1641,1119	478. A flower, enlarged.	A single open flower on its stalk, with five rounded petal-like sepals, the stamens and the ring of short styles in the centre.
479	1531,1801,1679,2025 - 1527,1988,1540,2025	479. Young fruit.	A young berry sitting in the spreading sepals, its top ribbed and puckered into segments around the short styles.
480	883,1797,1026,2025 - 879,1793,904,1828	480. Same, cut across.	The young fruit cut across, showing its ten cells arranged in a ring like the spokes of a wheel, above the sepals and stalk.
481	1561,1573,1684,1703	481. Seed divided lengthwise, and magnified.	A round seed split open, its coat enclosing the embryo curled round a pale central mass.
482	1395,1574,1532,1712	482. Embryo, more magnified.	The embryo taken out of the seed, curved round into a thick crescent or ring.
